    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0484" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg388"/>

                <head>No. 290.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Nelson to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-02-14"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 14, 1872</date>.
                        (Received March 1.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 514]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatches Nos. 504 and
                    507, I herewith inclose a copy and translation (A, B, and C) of another article
                    by Mr. Emilio Valasco, from the Siglo XIX, upon “Mexican relations with the
                    United States,” which is devoted to the history of the “Free Zone.” Though the
                    views expressed are at variance with those held both by the American and the
                    Mexican governments upon the subject, the position and antecedents of the writer
                    render his statements worthy of consideration.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS H. NELSON.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d290-a1.xml" xpointer="d290-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
